t approval starts stays held until every named [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]dependency finishes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]approval_wait_argument.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/approval_wait_argument.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-vs[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-vs/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared wait-spec parser and `sase bead work --wait`[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]bead_work_wait[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead_work_wait: add the shared `agent,bead=<id>` wait-spec parser and a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase bead work -w/--wait` option that renders the extra waits onto [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every unblocked epic segment.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Carry approval waits into the tale coder prompt[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tale_coder_wait[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tale_coder_wait: give `PlanApprovalResult` wait fields and stamp a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]canonical `%wait(...)` directive onto the approved tale's coder [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]successor prompt.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Thread a wait spec through the host-owned epic launch[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]epic_launch_wait[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bead_work_wait[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic_launch_wait: pass an optional wait spec from `prepare_epic_launch` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the epic launch monitor into the `sase bead work --wait` argv, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]including resume hints.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Accept `wait` on the plan gate approval options[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate_wait_input[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tale_coder_wait, epic_launch_wait[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate_wait_input: declare `wait` on the tale and epic approval option [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]schemas, validate it in the gate command, and route the parsed result [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]into the coder prompt and the epic launch.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]`sase plan approve --wait`[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]plan_approve_cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate_wait_input[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan_approve_cli: add a `-w/--wait` option to `sase plan approve` that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]validates the spec before anything is mutated and forwards it to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]approval executor.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Wait field in the ACE approval modal[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ace_approval_wait[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate_wait_input[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ace_approval_wait: add an editable wait row to the ACE custom-approval [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]modal and forward the spec through both the neutral and legacy ACE [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]approval paths.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-vs","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_i